1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Here's an arrow, one step to the right.

2
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:09,800
And another, one step straight up.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Each is exactly one square long.

4
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:19,500
We'll call them e one and e two.

5
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:22,300
In coordinates, that's one, zero,

6
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:25,200
and zero, one.

7
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:29,800
Everything else will be built from these two.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
What does the point three, two really mean?

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,500
Read the three as: stretch e one by three.

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,500
And the two says: stretch e two by two.

11
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:52,300
Now add them, tip to tail.

12
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,300
Right on our yellow dot.

13
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:58,600
So v is exactly that sum.

14
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:05,500
Three, two is three e one plus two e two.

15
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:09,700
Coordinates aren't just labels on a point.

16
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:13,200
They're instructions: stretch, stretch, then add.
